{},"On focus, the text switches to the editable form without separators. ",[284,360,361],{},"inputmode",[284,363,364],{},"numeric"," when ",[284,367,302],{},[284,369,306],{},[284,371,354],{},", and ",[284,374,302],{}," otherwise, so phones show the matching number keyboard.",[377,378,379,380,351,383,386,387,389,390,392,393,396,397,402,403,407],"tip",{},"The component has no ",[284,381,382],{},"min",[284,384,385],{},"max",". It is a text input underneath, so the native ",[284,388,382],{},", ",[284,391,385],{}," and ",[284,394,395],{},"step"," have no effect. Use ",[398,399,401],"a",{"href":400},"\u002Fgetting-started\u002Fform\u002Fvalidation","validation rules"," for ranges; see ",[398,404,406],{"href":405},"#with-form-validation","With form validation"," below.",[294,409,411],{"id":410},"unit","Unit",[281,413,414,415,348,417,419,420,423],{},"When ",[284,416,410],{},[284,418,310],{},", \"NTD\" is shown (\"元\" in Traditional Chinese, switching with the locale). The text can be changed in ",[398,421,47],{"href":422},"\u002Fgetting-started\u002Ftheme\u002Fmessages#overridable-items","; passing a string shows that text. Units vary in length, so the right padding follows the unit's actual width and the number never overlaps the unit.",[322,425],{"name":426},"input-number-unit",[281,428,429,392,431,433,434,438,439,441,442,444,445,287],{},[284,430,410],{},[284,432,314],{}," can also have site-wide defaults; see ",[398,435,437],{"href":436},"\u002Fgetting-started\u002Ftheme\u002Fcomponent-defaults#configurable-props","Configurable props",". The site-wide ",[284,440,410],{}," only accepts ",[284,443,310],{}," \u002F ",[284,446,306],{},[294,448,450],{"id":449},"variants","Variants",[281,452,453,454,389,457,392,460,463,464,287],{},"Uses the ",[284,455,456],{},"variant",[284,458,459],{},"color",[284,461,462],{},"highlight"," of ",[284,465,466],{},"UInput",[322,468],{"name":469},"input-number-variant",[294,471,473],{"id":472},"icon","Icon",[281,475,453,476,463,478,480],{},[284,477,472],{},[284,479,466],{},", shown on the left alongside the unit.",[322,482],{"name":483},"input-number-icon",[294,485,487],{"id":486},"size-and-states","Size and states",[281,489,490,491,494],{},"While loading, the spinner sits to the right of the unit and the number and unit move left to make room. See ",[398,492,87],{"href":493},"\u002Fcomponents\u002Foverview\u002Fcommon"," for the behavior shared by all states.",[322,496],{"name":497},"input-number-states",[289,499,501],{"id":500},"examples","Examples",[294,503,406],{"id":504},"with-form-validation",[281,506,507,508,511,512,392,515,518,519,522],{},"Use ",[284,509,510],{},"requiredNumber"," for required fields and add ranges with ",[284,513,514],{},"v.minValue",[284,516,517],{},"v.maxValue","; use ",[284,520,521],{},"optionalNonNegativeNumber"," for optional non-negative numbers. What gets validated and submitted is a number, without separators.",[322,524],{"name":525},"input-number-validation",[294,527,529],{"id":528},"centered-numbers","Centered numbers",[281,531,532,535,536,539,540,543],{},[284,533,534],{},"ui.base"," has a built-in ",[284,537,538],{},"text-right","; pass ",[284,541,542],{},"text-center"," to center the number, which suits short fields inside a sentence. With a unit or while loading, the right padding follows the trailing content's actual width, so the number never overlaps the unit.",[322,545],{"name":546},"input-number-center",[294,548,550],{"id":549},"clear-button","Clear button",[281,552,553,554,557,558,560,561,407],{},"Put a clear button in ",[284,555,556],{},"#trailing",". ",[284,559,556],{}," sits next to the unit and the loading icon without replacing them; see ",[398,562,564],{"href":563},"#slots","Slots",[322,566],{"name":567},"input-number-clearable",[294,569,571],{"id":570},"accessing-the-native-input","Accessing the native input",[281,573,574,575,578],{},"Get the native input through ",[284,576,577],{},"inputRef"," on the template ref.",[322,580],{"name":581},"input-number-exp